==Hausa==

===Etymology===
From a {{bor|ha|ber}} language; compare {{cog|mzb|tazeqqa}}. A {{cog|tmh|-}} origin is geographically more plausible, but no phonologically matching term is attested, and it would be unusual for a settled people to borrow a term related to settled life from nomads.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ha-IPA|taskā̀}}

===Noun===
{{ha-noun|f|taskā̀|taskōkī}}

# personal [[room]] of the head of the [[household]]
# [[storeroom]]
# [[safe]], [[strongbox]]

===References===
* {{R:ha:Kossmann 2005}}

